      "writtenOn": "2024-07-12T23:20:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The advice I\u0027m familiar with is to avoid const data members in C++:\n\n - https://quuxplusone.github.io/blog/2022/01/23/dont-const-all-the-things/#data-members-never-const\n - https://lesleylai.info/en/const-and-reference-member-variables/\n\nThe OutputLayerState class already has const data members, and LayerState contains OutputLayerState, so LayerStack is already restricted in some ways (i.e. no assignment, no swap, no moving-from).\n\nLayerStack doesn\u0027t contain LayerState directly but instead contains `std::vector\u003cLayerState\u003e`, so LayerStack still has swap and move-assignment, but not copy-assignment. Making mLayers const will disable swap and assignment for the LayerStack class, which also disables them for classes containing LayerStack (i.e. the Prediction and PromotionCandidate classes).\n\nMaking PromotionCandidate non-assignable causes a compile error in Predictor::promoteIfCandidate:\n\n```\n    auto candidateEntry \u003d getCandidateEntryByHash(predictionHash);\n    ...\n    mCandidates.erase(candidateEntry);\n```\n\ncandidateEntry is an iterator, and it is used to erase an entry from `std::deque\u003cPromotionCandidate\u003e mCandidates`. Erasing an entry shifts the remaining entries by one swap, which apparently needs swap or assignment.\n\nBuild error: https://paste.googleplex.com/5496974050852864\n\n`error: object of type \u0027android::compositionengine::impl::planner::Predictor::PromotionCandidate\u0027 cannot be assigned because its copy assignment operator is implicitly deleted`",
